                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/2115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Counselor of Embassy in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-18T13:00:00-05:00">October 18, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>285. Your 618, October 12, 4 p.m. The Department authorizes you to instruct
                    Tsingtao that it is authorized to inform American citizens that, although they
                    are under no legal obligation to furnish the information requested on the form
                    prepared by the local authorities, they may voluntarily comply with the request
                    for information by furnishing such data as they wish to furnish.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
